  "schema": {
    "description": "The OWL counterpart of delivery-ops.oont.yaml, modeling the same last-mile delivery domain (depots, vehicles, drivers, customers, shipments, delivery stops) so the two styles can be compared side by side. Both describe what exists and how it is connected — here, shipment S-5001 is delayed because van V-101 is in maintenance. OWL, however, has no first-class notion of 'actions': it can state that S-5001 is delayed, but not that an agent may call assignVehicle with validations and side effects. That gap is the point of comparison.",
